/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Electric vehicles \(EVs\) are automobiles powered by electric motors instead of internal combustion engines. They use rechargeable battery packs to store and supply energy, eliminating the need for gasoline or diesel. EVs are designed to provide a cleaner, more energy-efficient alternative to traditional vehicles, reducing carbon emissions and dependence on fossil fuels. With advancements in technology, EVs have become more practical, offering longer driving ranges, faster charging times, and improved performance.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
